course: dictionary
lesson: 8274
title: Rigid: stiff, strict, and not bending
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rigid means stiff and hard. A rigid thing does not bend easily. Think of a wooden ruler or a metal spoon: you can feel that they will not bend. Rigid is also used for rules and plans that are strict and cannot be changed, and for people who will not change their ideas.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «A frightened or angry dog goes stiff and still: its tail may be tucked low or held high and rigid.» The words stiff and still tell you rigid means not moving or bending. Now try it: if you swap in stiff, the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: In a story, «rigid with fear» means so scared that you cannot move. The fear makes your body go stiff. Engineers use the idea too: «Adding a diagonal strut to a square frame divides it into two triangles and makes it rigid.» The strut stops the frame from bending or wobbling.
fact: Rigid means stiff and hard, and does not bend easily.
fact: Rigid rules and plans are strict and cannot be changed.
fact: A rigid person will not change their ideas or habits.
fact: Rigid materials such as wood, metal and hard plastic keep their shape.
fact: Flexible is the opposite of rigid: rubber and fabric bend.
exercise: «Adding a diagonal strut to a square frame divides it into two triangles and makes it rigid.» What does rigid mean here? | Bendy, like rubber | Very fast | *Stiff, so it will not bend easily | Painted in bright colours
exercise: Which material is rigid? | Rubber | Thin paper that flaps in the wind | Fabric | *Hard plastic
exercise: In a story, a girl stood «rigid with fear». What does this mean? | Fast asleep | *Too scared to move | Very happy and dancing | Hungry for lunch
test: «A frightened or angry dog goes stiff and still: its tail may be tucked low or held high and rigid.» What does rigid mean in this sentence? | Wagging very fast | *Stiff and not moving | Floppy and loose | Painted gold
test: The club had «rigid rules» that could never be changed. What does rigid mean here? | Made of wood | Very short | *Strict and not able to change | Kind and gentle
exam: Which word is the noun form of rigid? | flexible | rigidly | stiffen | *rigidity
